      "category": "Text",
      "text": "§ 3. *Chief Administrative Law Judge.* The Chief Administrative Law Judge shall be an attorney admitted to practice in the State of New York and appointed by the Mayor who shall have the following responsibilities in addition to presiding over administrative trials and hearings:",
